meta {
  name: Start transfer (as consumer)
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{mgmtUrl}}/v1/transfers
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "agreementId": "{{mgmtAgreementId}}",
    "format": "HttpData-PULL"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.body && res.body.consumerPid) {
    bru.setVar("mgmtTransferConsumerPid", res.body.consumerPid);
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 201
}

docs {
  The consumer's management API, not the DSP endpoint POST /transfers/request: the body
  is a StartTransfer (agreementId, and format, default HttpData-PULL), not a
  TransferRequestMessage. The connector sends the DSP message to the provider of that
  agreement in the background. The answer is 201 with the transfer as the connector sees
  it (consumerPid, state REQUESTED, agreementId, format).
  Use the "two-connectors" environment. Negotiate first ("Start negotiation"), then
  "Get negotiation" saves mgmtAgreementId. The weather-stations data is served by
  scripts/dev-identities.sh (portitor:source in examples/datasets.json).
  Saves mgmtTransferConsumerPid. Debug: management.rs and transfer.rs (crates/portitor-connector/src).
}
